## Authentication
Cookie-based (session-id) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (2)
- `GET /{id}/{1Id}/{remote-weblab-triggerId}/oe/{oeToken}` — Authenticate with a remote web lab trigger.
- `GET /{id}/batch/{batchId}/op/{opToken}` — Authenticate with an operation token.

### Data Read (9)
- `GET /{id}` — Read data for a specific item.
- `GET /{id}/{1c5c1ecf7303Id}/{d6a7a58005ecId}/inputs` — Read inputs for a specific item.
- `GET /ad/u` — Retrieve ad-related information.
- `GET /api/v1/dsync/amazon` — Get Amazon data synchronization status.
- `GET /customer/v1/bs_img_service` — Get customer image service data.
- `GET /gh/useracquisition` — Get user acquisition data.
- `GET /ifh/inflowcomponent` — Fetch inflow component data.
- `GET /marketingtracking/v1/sync` — Synchronize marketing tracking data.
- `GET /puff/content` — Retrieve content from puff.

### Search (1)
- `GET /sch/ajax/autocomplete` — Get search autocompletion suggestions.

